      "text": "Major Global Weather Events — October 19 to 21, 2025\n\nTurkey (Oct 20): Heavy rains in Payas, Hatay, caused flooding, blocked highways, and damaged homes.\n\nSouth Sudan (Oct 21): Floods affected 900,000+ people, worsening the humanitarian crisis.\n\nPhilippines (Oct 19–20): Tropical Storm Ramil killed 7+, displaced 13,700+, and damaged infrastructure.\n\nFrance (Oct 20): Tornado hit Val-d’Oise, uprooting trees, toppling cranes, and causing power outages.\n\nUK (Oct 19): Northern Ireland hit by heavy rain, severe flooding in County Down.\n\nLibya (Oct 19): Thunderstorms with hail struck northwest regions, damaging streets and property.\n\nSouth Africa (Oct 19): Severe storms with hail and wind in North West, Gauteng, Limpopo.\n\nVenezuela (Oct 19): Rivers overflowed in Sucre State, flooding Cumanacoa and San Fernando de Tataracual.\n\nIndonesia (Oct 21): Rain-triggered lahar on Mount Semeru blocked roads and carried volcanic debris",
